  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Show that the sum of $2n$ consecutive integers is divisible by $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$S=n(2k+2n+1)$, so the sum is divisible by $n$.\n\nWrite the integers as $k+1,k+2,\\ldots,k+2n$, sum them and factor out $n$.",
      "worked": "Let the integers be $k+1,k+2,\\ldots,k+2n$, where $k$ is an integer and $n$ is a positive integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sum_{i=1}^{2n}(k+i)&=2nk+\\sum_{i=1}^{2n}i\\\\\\sum_{i=1}^{2n}(k+i)&=2nk+\\frac{(2n)(2n+1)}{2}\\\\\\sum_{i=1}^{2n}(k+i)&=2nk+n(2n+1)\\\\\\sum_{i=1}^{2n}(k+i)&=n(2k+2n+1).\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $2k+2n+1$ is an integer, the sum is divisible by $n$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
